# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Provider accounts (PyKeyStore-backed)
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Each provider can have multiple accounts — Sophia rotates across
# them using the strategy in `strategies.model-provider-selection` (the
# provider-pool picks the next from the rotation queue per request).
# Accounts are stored in Sophia's PyKeyStore vault, not in this file.
# To add an account:
#
#   docker compose -f docker-compose.cluster.yml exec -T sophia \
#     python -m sophia.cmds.manage_secrets set anthropic_api_key
#     # (paste sk-ant-... when prompted — Sophia reads from stdin,
#     #  the entrypoint already initialized the vault)
#
# The env_key field on each provider (e.g. "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY") is
# the lookup key Sophia uses when populating the Authorization header.
# If you add multiple accounts for the same provider, use suffixes:
#   anthropic_api_key        (account 1, default)
#   anthropic_api_key_2      (account 2)
#   anthropic_api_key_3      (account 3)
# Sophia reads them in suffix order and rotates via the strategy.
#
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# How to test with this config
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. Fill in the providers + enabled models above.
# 2. Add one or more accounts per enabled provider via manage_secrets.
# 3. Open http://127.0.0.1:3000 in a browser → Open WebUI loads with
#    Sophia as the backend (OPENAI_API_BASE_URL=http://sophia:8765/v1).
# 4. The Models dropdown shows every enabled model from every
#    provider; the Strategy dropdown lets you pick the rotation
#    strategy from the `strategies.model-provider-selection` list.
# 5. Hit Send on a chat and watch sophia_1's docker logs — you'll see
#    `[SophiaPool] chat via <provider> <model> via <account>` lines
#    showing the rotation in action. Per-request usage rows are
#    written to /var/lib/sophia/sophia.db (visible via the
#    /v1/usage/summary endpoint with a `collection` or `admin` role).
#
# 6. Confirm the rotation is happening by sending the same prompt N
#    times and checking /v1/usage/by_provider?requestor=openwebui —
#    each call should land on a different account until the rotation
#    cycles. With one account per provider you'll see the strategy
#    picking the cheapest / least-used / round-robin across PROVIDERS
#    rather than across accounts.